For $\pi/3<\epsilon<4\pi/3$ we have the same Jordan cell, $\mathcal J_0(f_\epsilon)=\{(\kappa^1,\operatorname{id})\}$, two $0$-barcodes and one $1$-barcode, that is, $\mathcal B_0(f_\epsilon)=\{[4\pi/3-\epsilon,2\pi/3+\epsilon),(4\pi/3-\epsilon,2\pi/3+\epsilon]\}$, and $\mathcal B_1(f_\epsilon)=\{[4\pi/3-\epsilon,2\pi/3+\epsilon]\}$.
